pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% `output EQUIOPTIMAL` stays available after `solx`, but its `FOR obj < ...`
% qualifier has to name the value below which nothing was removed. The excluded
% x1=0 class contains a solution of objective 0, so the honest qualifier is
% `FOR obj < 0` — it used to print `FOR obj < 100`, the logged representative's
% value, which is false: restricted to obj < 100 the input still has a solution
% while the output formula has none. The verdict string itself is pinned in
% `tests/solution_logging_verdicts.rs`.
f 1;
solx ~x1 x2;
output EQUIOPTIMAL FILE;
conclusion NONE;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
